cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its reported results, please cite this repository and record the commit used."
type: software
title: "SETI silence audit: From radio nondetection to conditional physical-arrival risk"
authors:
  - family-names: Legotin
    given-names: Artem
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-02"
repository-code: "https://github.com/arlegotin/seti-silence-audit"
url: "https://github.com/arlegotin/seti-silence-audit"
license:
  - AGPL-3.0-only
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Reproducible research software auditing whether the UCLA 2020–2023 Green Bank
  Telescope radio nondetection narrows physical-arrival risk within the next
  100 years in a declared finite scenario family. Uses the published primary
  target geometry, 61 physical sites with linked repeated observations, bounded
  observing times, assumed detector response, interacting expansion simulations
  and an independent-site comparison. Persistent bright emission gives an upper
  risk envelope of roughly 11 percent before the null and 4 percent after it
  under the nominal detector; invisible counterparts prevent full-family
  contraction. These are conditional model results, not calibrated real-world
  arrival probabilities. Includes frozen evidence, uncertainty accounting,
  robustness comparisons, review corrections and offline report reconstruction.
keywords:
  - SETI
  - technosignatures
  - nondetection
  - physical arrival
  - reproducible research
